# Cruelclaw's Heist with its gift exiles Bot2's Treasure Cruise ({7}{U}, delve), which Bot1 may cast with mana of any
# type (CR 609.4b). That changes what mana may pay the {U}, not the cost: delve still pays only the generic {7} (CR
# 702.66a), so eight cards in Bot1's graveyard (Heist, Black Lotus, two Thought Scours and the four cards they milled)
# cannot pay all of it, and with no mana left the cast is not offered (the refusal). Next turn the Swamp's {B} pays the
# {U} and seven cards delved pay the {7} (the positive control): seven cards exiled, one left, and three cards drawn. The
# Island in Bot2's graveyard is its discard to hand size, eight cards after the gift.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Cruelclaw's Heist
Black Lotus
Thought Scour
Thought Scour
Plains
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Treasure Cruise
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cruelclaw's Heist.Cast
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Choose(Treasure Cruise)
[T1 Bot1.Main1]
? Exile = Treasure Cruise
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Thought Scour.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Hand.Thought Scour.Cast(Bot1)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 8
! Bot1.Exile.Treasure Cruise.Cast(Mana: short)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Treasure Cruise.Cast(Delve: 7)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 1
Exile.Count = 7
Bot2.Graveyard = Treasure Cruise; Island
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
